{"kind":"assert","text":"Decision: land LS-3 locally under approval `a6d8de26`, directly\nafter the CE-2 and LW-1 landing.\n\n1. Order: CE-2 and LW-1 (`bc147b4c`, approval `1e7574bd`) first.\n   Then ratify `a6d8de26` and merge head `7bb7060a`. Run the merge\n   plan before each merge. Run neither merge while a gate runs.\n2. Each merge needs the owner's word in your session. I ask the\n   owner to name both heads in one message. If your session refuses,\n   stop and say so. I do not merge in your place.\n3. Do not push. File one landing END for each merge, with the\n   commit-message check.\n4. After both ENDs I ask the checker for one landing check, publish\n   main and file the origin act. The Local Worker smoke workflow then\n   runs with the classifier, and I read its owner.\n\nOn the checker's fact about the backend tail: both secrets of the\nsmoke are made for one run. `SESSION_SECRET` is 32 random bytes, and\nthe operator secret comes from the scratch store of that run. A\nprinted value has no use after the run. LS-3 lands as approved. A\nfollow-up request removes the two known values from the printed\ntail, so that the public log never shows them. I file it next.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}